the Trump organization is rejecting a  new claim of profiteering during former  president Trump's time in the office the  house oversight committee says Trump  owned hotels charged excessive rates  sometimes more than one thousand dollars  a night for a room for Secret Service  Personnel protecting the Trump family  Scott McFarland is on Capitol Hill with  more on this story so good morning to  you Scott the question I have is how  much is excessive  now according to the records newly  released by Congress Gail the Trump  hotels and properties charge the Secret  Service as much as five times the  Government rate for some accommodations  over the course of four years that  amounted to more than 1.4 million  dollars in tax money that went to the  Trump organization in one case the  Secret Service was charged more than  eleven hundred dollars for a room at the  Trump International Hotel here in  Washington for agents protecting Trump's  son Eric in March 2017. that's well  above the 242 dollars allowed under the  Government rate committee documents also  reference agent visits to Trump's  Bedminster Golf Club in Mar-A-Lago while  citing a statement from Eric Trump in  2019 that the Secret Service effectively  stays at Trump properties for free and  saves the government money  the committee says there may also be  other expenses it hasn't seen yet  they've asked the Secret Service for a  complete list of taxpayer-funded  expenses at Trump properties and the  agency tells CBS News it will respond to  the panel in a statement to CBS News  Eric Trump stands by his claim that the  arrangement was for at Cost discounted  and free stays and says the  organizations would have made more money  by selling services to full paying  guests Nate  Scott thank you
 

